  "description": "Drop in and get rowdy. The Rossignol DH Project downhill mountain bike is purpose-built for aggressive gravity runs at your favorite resort. From its hydroformed aluminum frame to its handpicked downhill components, it's designed to hit send lap after lap. The mullet layout with a 27.5-inch wheel in the rear and a 29-inch wheel in the front keeps it nimble and aggressive in steep, technical terrain. Crankworx Whip-Off approved, it's the tool of choice for going big thanks to a 200 mm Rockshox Vivid Coil rear shock and a 200 mm dual-crown Boxxer fork. You can count on the set-it-and-forget simplicity and pure braking power of the SRAM DB8 four-piston brakes when it comes time to check your speed. Set yourself up for endless park laps Stuff, Durable Downhill Performance 6061 hydroformed aluminum frame with 200 mm travel Horst-Link four-bar rear suspension platform for aggressive downhill riding. Double Crown, Race-Level Fork Performance RockShox Boxxer 200 mm Fork with double crown and 38 mm chassis balances stiffness and ride quality to deliver race-level downhill performance. World-Class Downhill Suspension A 200 mm Rockshox Vivid Coil rear shock packs the bottomless feel of a high-performance coil shock for lapping the bike park, charging rowdy descents and hitting gaps. Four-Piston Braking Power, Easy Maintenance SRAM DB8 Stealth brakes deliver smooth modulation, set-it-and-forget-it simplicity and the unmatched braking power and control of a four-piston caliper paired with a 220 mm front rotor and a 200 mm rear rotor. Precise, Reliable Shifting Under Pressure SRAM GX DH 7-Speed shifting is purpose-built for downhill riding, offering precise, reliable shifts when they matter most.",
